1**, not the newest tag. On npm, `prisma`'s `latest` tag points to a release candidate, `8.0.0-rc.33`. But `latest` for `@prisma/client` and `@prisma/adapter-pg` is 7.10.1, and the command-line tool and client have to be the same version. So I pinned all three to 7.10.1, the newest stable release. If you'd rather have the 8.0 release candidate, say so and I'll switch.\n\nWhat I added:\n- **Packages:** `@prisma/client`, `@prisma/adapter-pg` (Prisma 7 needs this to connect to PostgreSQL) and `dotenv`, plus `prisma` as a dev dependency.\n- **`prisma.config.ts`:** reads `DATABASE_URL` from `.env`.\n- **`prisma/schema.prisma`:**\n  - `User`: unique `email`, optional `name`.\n  - `Post`: `title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to false, and a required author.\n- **Tables:** created by an initial migration, saved in `prisma/migrations/`.\n- **Generated client:** written to `src/generated/prisma`, which I added to `.gitignore`. After a fresh `npm install`, run `npx prisma generate` before the script.\n- **`script.ts`:** creates `alice@example.com` with one published post and one draft. It skips creating them if Alice already exists, so it can be run again despite the unique email.\n\n**Install warning:** npm blocked the packages' install scripts, including the one for `@prisma/engines`. The migration and client generation still worked. If a clean install has trouble, run `npm install-scripts approve @prisma/engines`.\n\n`src/index.ts` still uses its in-memory storage; I didn't move it to the database. Everything is written up in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed.","ttft_ms":4541,"type":"result","duration_ms":119494,"uuid":"f013f5c9-e51d-444d-91a5-a446f6da4678","ttft_stream_ms":3458,"time_to_request_ms":657,"first_content_frame_ms":3458,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":4357,"cacheReadInputTokens":262470,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11389,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.23083